<title>USA: Republicans let Clinton present budget on Feb. 6.</title>
<headline>Republicans let Clinton present budget on Feb. 6.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Republican leaders said they will agree to permit President Clinton to submit his fiscal 1998 budget Feb. 6 instead of Feb. 3, the legally required deadline.</p>
<p>Senate Republican Conference chairman Connie Mack of Florida told reporters the president's State of the Union address to a joint session of the House and Senate would be held Feb. 4.</p>
<p>Mack and Senate Republican Whip Don Nickles of Oklahoma spoke to reporters after a meeting of the Senate Republicans.</p>
